 #edb/ref 17592186049596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1031 "Constructing Algebraic Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1033 3721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051009 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7931e951-f0f8-5132-97e2-67fa64802a65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228877 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228877 #edb/ref 1071 "According to a recent report, $40\\%$ of viewers said they enjoyed documentaries. Of those, $50\\%$ preferred documentaries about nature. What percentage of all viewers preferred nature documentaries?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228877 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f528740-2fa6-5441-ab8b-86ce294dbf75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228877 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $x$ be the total number of viewers.\n\nWe're told that $40\\%$ of viewers enjoyed documentaries. Thus, the number of viewers who enjoy documentaries is \n\n$$\n0.4x.\n$$\n\nWe are also told that of those viewers who enjoy documentaries, $50\\%$ preferred nature topics. So, the number of viewers who preferred nature documentaries is\n\n$$\n0.50(0.4x) = 0.20x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.20x$ represents $20\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $20\\%$ of all viewers preferred nature documentaries." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228882 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228882 #edb/ref 1071 "A service adjusted a subscription fee to $90\\%$ of its original cost. A surcharge of $18\\%$ was applied to the adjusted fee. If the subscription originally cost $\\[math]180,$ what is the surcharge?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228882 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97d0ab51-97cd-5781-be30-4d70adc5d214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228882 #edb/ref 1074 "First, the adjusted fee is $90\\%$ of the original cost $(\\[math]180){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90%\\times 180 & =\\frac{90}{100}\\times 180 \\\\  & =0.9\\times 180 \\\\  & =162\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the adjusted fee is $\\[/math]162.$ Then, the surcharge is $18\\%$ of this fee:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18%\\times 162 & =\\frac{18}{100}\\times 162 \\\\  & =0.18\\times 162 \\\\  & =29.16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surcharge is $\\[math]29.16.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228884 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228884 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $160\\%$ of $75,$ and then $150\\%$ of the result." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228884 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "91ca6940-1bc7-583b-8bac-81d7da934167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228884 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find $160\\%$ of $75{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160%\\times 75 & =\\frac{160}{100}\\times 75 \\\\  & =1.6\\times 75 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $150\\%$ of the result $(120){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150%\\times 120 & =\\frac{150}{100}\\times 120 \\\\  & =1.5\\times 120 \\\\  & =180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $180.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186486434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186486452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229193 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying Subsequent Perc